<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Utico lifts half-year, wary on prospects.</title>
<headline>Utico lifts half-year, wary on prospects.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     116	   vs  111</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  58	   vs  55</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   7.03	  vs  6.72</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  11.34	  vs  12.06</p>
<p>    Tax			 4.32	  vs  5.35</p>
<p>    Interest received     2.58	  vs  6.73</p>
<p>    Turnover		186.86	  vs  186.33</p>
<p>Div payable October 4</p>
<p>on register September 20</p>
<p>Full name: Utico Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Tobacco group Utico said high excise duties, new trading restrictions, smuggling and slower economic growth had lead to a fall in domestic cigarette market volumes. These problems would continue in the second half and the group's performance would be adversely affected, it cautioned.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
